### Control ownership

| Plane | Accountable owner | Pack responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| Semantic/model construction | `dsrust-pack` | Closed vocabulary, exact-source compatibility, deterministic projection |
| Supply chain | Marketplace + consumer CI | Pin source identity; verify archive/receipt; consumer pins crate/lockfile |
| Compilation | Consumer CI | Pack emits source; consumer must run Rust compiler and policy gates |
| Model/provider access | Consumer platform | No credentials in RDF/templates; provider IAM and egress stay outside pack |
| Tool execution | Consumer application | Generated tool seams fail until explicitly implemented |
| Data governance | Consumer data platform | Prompts, examples, responses, PII, residency, retention remain consumer-owned |
| Runtime SLO/DR | Consumer SRE/platform | Define service SLIs/SLOs, capacity, regions, RTO/RPO in enterprise architecture |
| Promotion/rollback | Enterprise delivery | Promote only with receipts; roll back by pinned-source regeneration |

### Promotion decision

This pack's marketplace qualification proves deterministic **construction**. It does not by itself
prove Rust compilation or production runtime behavior. Promotion beyond source generation therefore
requires consumer-owned compiler/test/security evidence attached to the enterprise asset.
